  "gaps": [
    "The three PLATEAU-derived public anchors locate the B1 approaches. Exact fare thresholds, paid endpoints and North/Metropolitan public seam coordinates are GAPs. Central 1's existing opening tie is weaker than Central 2's.",
    "1F and 2F labels are sourced. Their z_m values are nominal render heights. Exact platform centerlines, widths, lengths, paid concourse shapes and device landings are GAPs.",
    "The connector records describe preview adjacency and device categories. Exact counts, landing positions, escalator directions and gate hours are GAPs. The south paid hall groups shared access from Central 1 and South.",
    "The indexed Toshima 2F–B1 PDF was readable as text. Direct retrieval returned 404. The JR East B1 diagram image returned 403. Retain facts-only provenance and confirm detailed device placements in the field.",
    "R1 is context only (OD-17). N02 gives visual rail context. MLIT R2 newer indoor data is login-gated. The JR–Tobu paid transfer opening is unresolved in the station inventory.",
    "Platform services record the regular JY, JA and JS assignments. The ward sheet also names Narita Express. Limited-express and exceptional track assignments need a dated per-track source."
  ]
